--- Test framework contract (ADR-0092).
---
--- This file is the stable op/cap contract for the handl test framework:
--- `test.run`, `property.for_all`, `benchmark.run`, `fuzz.run`,
--- `snapshot.*`. `assert` is a keyword, not a library op, and is handled
--- directly by the eval engine.
--- `handl-plugin-lib-test` is deleted; the `handl "..." = rust_*` bindings
--- below resolve to the temporary Rust handls hosted in
--- `plugin-engine-test::framework` (`src/framework/`) until the stdlib
--- primitives the pure-handl implementations need land:
--- error raise/capture (snapshot.match, test.run), a seeded RNG reachable
--- from handl (property/fuzz), and a clock (benchmark).
---
--- test.run — run a test suite (array of test cases) and return a report.
--- property.for_all — run a property-based test with seeded RNG for count iterations.
--- benchmark.run — benchmark a function for a number of iterations and return a timing report.
--- fuzz.run — run a function with random inputs for count iterations and report failures.
--- snapshot.format — serialize a value to a pretty-printed JSON string.
--- snapshot.match — assert that an actual value matches an expected snapshot.
cap "test.run"
cap "property.for_all"
cap "benchmark.run"
cap "fuzz.run"
cap "snapshot.format"
cap "snapshot.match"
op "test.run" : Array -> Value
  guarantee: True
op "property.for_all" : (Function, Number) -> Bool
  guarantee: True
op "benchmark.run" : (Function, Number) -> Value
  guarantee: True
op "fuzz.run" : (Function, Number) -> Value
  guarantee: True
op "snapshot.format" : Value -> String
  guarantee: IsString(output)
op "snapshot.match" : (String, Value, Value) -> Bool
  guarantee: True

handl "test.run" = rust_test_run
handl "property.for_all" = rust_property_for_all
handl "benchmark.run" = rust_benchmark_run
handl "fuzz.run" = rust_fuzz_run
handl "snapshot.format" = rust_snapshot_format
handl "snapshot.match" = rust_snapshot_match
